CRITICAL SECTION ->
        A segment of the code that access a shared resources that must not be accessed concurrently accessed by more than one thread.

RACE CONDITION ->
        A bug that occurs when the output of the program depends on the unpredictable sequence or timings of the thread.
        (When multiple thread are working on a shared resource and their timings overlap only one of the multiple gets the shared value changed)

MUTUAL EXCLUSION ->
        It ensures that only one thread can enter the critical section at a time.
